  "content": {
    "id": "p77-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Explain why we can find the LCM of two numbers by multiplying them then dividing by the HCF.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "For each prime factor, the smallest and largest powers together give the powers in both numbers. Hence $\\mathrm{HCF}\\times\\mathrm{LCM}=a\\times b$, so $\\mathrm{LCM}=a\\times b\\div\\mathrm{HCF}$.",
      "worked": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p77-q15-worked-reason",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "For each prime factor, use index 0 if it is absent from a number. The HCF uses the smaller index and the LCM uses the larger index. These two indices add to the sum of the indices in the original numbers. Thus multiplying the HCF and LCM gives the same prime factors, with the same powers, as multiplying the two numbers.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p77-q15-worked-identity",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "right",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "For two numbers ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "a",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "b",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\mathrm{HCF}\\times\\mathrm{LCM}=a\\times b",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p77-q15-worked-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "right",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "So, ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\mathrm{LCM}=a\\times b\\div\\mathrm{HCF}",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
